HRX native distribution

libamdf and Loom derive from HRX/IREE under Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception.
The C++ importer includes Roberto Raggi's MIT-licensed cplusplus parser.
CORE-MATH and AMD ISA tables retain their MIT notices; HSA headers retain NCSA.
Linux syscall headers retain their original notices and syscall exception.
All component license texts and header notices accompany the libraries.
The hrx-rs bridge is MIT licensed.

Modified source, patches and build recipes:
https://github.com/zacharydenton/hrx-rs/releases/download/native-20261008-7e9c7bbd5e/hrx-native-sources.tar.gz
SHA-256: 8e6b81d2b8b6614fb6d8a7e9a43c2d6da2c132cc172adfe17b0f506d10e5aada

Benchmark fixtures in native/qualification derive from krea2-hrx (MIT),
and arcface-hrx and h3-hrx (Apache-2.0); exact revisions and license texts accompany those files.

Resident exchange, workgroup race, and GPU file-I/O fixtures in tests/kernels and
tests/support/resident_routes.rs derive from libamdf CTS at HRX 7e9c7bbd5e
under Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception; original notices are retained.
The io_uring Rust layouts derive from the pinned Linux syscall headers;
regenerate them with scripts/generate-storage-bindings.py.
